also, any ways to prioritize french covers for movies and shows?

Yes. The best method is to replace the current Metahub poster URLs with direct French poster URLs.

Right now, each title uses:

"poster": "https://images.metahub.space/poster/medium/tt24070754/img"
Metahub chooses its own default artwork, so the cover may be English, textless, or occasionally from another region. Stremio displays whatever URL is placed in each catalog item’s poster field, so we can explicitly choose French artwork instead. 

Best approach
For every movie and series:

Match the IMDb ID to its TMDB entry.

Request available posters with French prioritized.

Select in this order:

French poster, language fr

Textless poster, language null

Original-language poster

Existing Metahub poster as a final fallback

Put the selected direct image URL into the catalog JSON.

TMDB supports language-specific movie and TV artwork, including French posters, through its image endpoints and include_image_language parameter. 

The resulting entry would look like:

{
  "id": "tt24070754",
  "type": "movie",
  "name": "Je verrai toujours vos visages",
  "poster": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/FRENCH_POSTER_FILE.jpg"
}
This would prioritize French covers inside the Top French catalog grid. When a title is opened, Stremio may still load some detailed metadata or background artwork from Cinemeta because the addon uses IMDb IDs and does not currently provide its own meta resource. 

So there are two levels:

Catalog covers only: replace the poster URLs in the two existing JSON files. This is simple and works with GitHub Pages.

French artwork throughout the detail pages: create a dynamic addon with a meta endpoint. That cannot be handled fully by the current static GitHub Pages structure.

For this addon, I recommend updating the catalog posters only. It preserves the simple one-URL installation and should make almost all visible movie and series covers French.


