logged in in TMDB - how to proceed from there?

From TMDB on your computer:

Click your profile picture → Settings.

Open API in the left menu.

If no API credentials exist, select Create or Request an API Key.

Choose Developer and accept the terms.

For the application form, you can enter:

Application name: Top French Stremio Addon

Application URL: https://github.com/A-A-prod/top-frenchmovies

Application summary: Personal Stremio catalog addon that displays French movies and series with French-language posters.

Once approved, return to Settings → API.

Copy the long value labelled API Read Access Token. Do not copy the shorter API Key. TMDB documents this long token as the Bearer token used for application authentication. 

Then on Windows:

Download and unzip the French-poster-ready package.

Open the extracted folder.

Click the address bar in File Explorer, type cmd, and press Enter.

Run:

python update_french_posters.py PASTE_YOUR_LONG_TOKEN_HERE
For example:

python update_french_posters.py eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9...
Do not put quotation marks around it unless Windows reports a parsing problem.

When it finishes, you should see:

Finished. Updated ___ posters; ___ retained their existing fallback.
Then upload these two newly modified files to GitHub, replacing the existing versions:

catalog/movie/top-french-movies.json
catalog/series/top-french-series.json
Do not share the token here or commit it to GitHub. The script uses it only while making the TMDB requests and does not save it inside either catalog file.


